====================================================================================================
V5 -- THE VERDICTS
====================================================================================================
  [FAIL] V1 [the pooled collapse scatter < 0.15 dex -- the PREDICTION] rms of log10 R about the binned-median curve at fixed x, full sample (T500_vir primary; T500_emp consistency row 0.325 dex)
         measured: rms = 0.313 dex (all 96 points; grid-bin rms 0.298 dex) vs the 0.15-dex gate; the falsifier sits at 0.3 (1.04 of the falsifier line)
  [PASS] V2 [V2: the outlier count and the list] clusters departing the pooled curve by > 3 sigma
         measured: 0 of 12 depart at the cluster-mean level (list: none); 0 with a single bin > 3 sigma (none)
  [PASS] V3 [the honest statement] coherent/mixed verdict + the clean subset
         measured: THE SAMPLE IS MIXED ON THE FRAMEWORK'S OWN TEST -- and the reading is STRUCTURALLY SINGLE, CURVE-FAILING.  (i) The 12 ratio-profiles do NOT collapse onto one curve at the predicted level: the pooled scatter of log10 R at fixed x = 0.313 dex (T500_vir) / 0.325 dex (T500_emp), ~2.1x the <0.15-dex prediction, sitting AT the P5 falsifier line (0.3 dex).  (ii) The scatter is NOT concentrated: 0 of 12 clusters depart by > 3 sigma (max cluster-mean 0.65 sigma, A3266; max single bin 2.46 sigma) and the departures show only a weak positive correlate with f_gas(420) (rho = +0.50, p = 0.10; M500 p = 0.22, kTvir p = 0.35, and the ordering shifts under the T500_emp calibration) -- the scatter is sample-wide, the mark of a per-cluster LEVELS spread (per-cluster rms 0.22-0.45 dex), not of scrambled profiles.  (iii) The CONTROL decides what kind of objects these are: at FIXED radius the 12 systems scatter only 0.079 dex (median over 8 radii, range 0.063-0.159), with the OUTERMOST bins the tightest (0.089 dex at 600 kpc) -- the systems ARE single equilibrium structures in the standard self-similar sense (Ghirardini+19's own minimum-scatter window), NOT line-of-sight superpositions, which would scramble the ratio-profiles far beyond this.  (iv) The framework's collapse-in-x fails because R carries the sample-wide dark-to-baryon ratio x (2.0-37.6) with the per-cluster offsets the registered amplitude input (the free-dust normalization, G075/G012) already owns: the G104 aperture power law (kTvir/T_floor at R500, f = 3.2-7.0) collapses at 0.05 dex because the aperture aligns each cluster at its own R500; the PROFILE-level x-space version filters no such level out and fails at 0.31 dex.  CLEAN SUBSET for the framework's tests (clusters whose own 8-bin rms about the pooled curve stays < 0.15 dex, T500_vir): 0 of 12 -- none; the aperture-level subset (G104's f = 3.2-7.0 power law, 0.05 dex) remains all 12.
         reading : V1 FAIL (0.31/0.32 dex vs 0.15, at the 0.3 falsifier), V2 PASS (0 outliers), the r-space control V2c PASS (0.04-0.18 dex): SINGLE STRUCTURES whose sample-wide dark-to-baryon spread defeats the framework's specific x-universality at the profile level

